CatalogueViewerPage ..> LocaleProvider

' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' DESIGN NOTES
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

note bottom of ModuleRequest
    Existing WEB01 contract injected into each feature adapter.
    Feature adapters use this contract instead of importing
    the shared apiClient directly.
end note

note bottom of RequireRole
    WEB03 controls visibility of role-restricted actions.
    The back end remains responsible for enforcing
    authorization on every protected operation.
end note

note bottom of CustomerDTO
    Customer contact information and dietary restrictions
    must only be displayed to roles authorized for those
    responsibilities, respecting confidentiality rules.
end note

note bottom of ProductDTO
    Product composition is represented through product
    references and quantities. Nested composition,
    allergen information and availability are derived
    according to the backend business rules.
end note

note bottom of ComponentSizeConfigurationDTO
    The configuration is identified by the combination
    of productId and sizeId, not by an independent ID.
end note

note bottom of CatalogueViewerPage
    Catalogue reading is public. Catalogue responses
    must not expose stock quantities or personal data.
end note

note bottom of ApiError
    API errors are presented through WEB04 feedback
    conventions. Validation details are shown when
    provided by the backend response.
end note

@enduml
